  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "Householder",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed boundary fencing, given its height and location, would have a detrimental impact on highway safety for pedestrians and road users, contrary to Policies DM1.B(g) and DM42.F of the Harrow Development Management Polices Local Plan (2013).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "The proposed front boundary fencing, due to the increased height and scale, would disrupt the openness of the streetscape by creating a walling or enclosure effect contrary to the existing character and appearance of the streetscene and surrounding area. Thus the proposal would not be in keeping with, and results in harm to, the character and appearance of the existing dwellinghouse, the streetscene and the surrounding area. The proposal therefore fails to comply with National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies D3.D (1) and (11) of the London Plan (2021), Core Policy CS1.B of the Harrow Core Strategy (2012), policy DM1 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013), and the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010)."
  ],
